    "title": "Jari Askins to serve as interim city attorney in Lawton - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Connor Nielsen ,\n2 hours ago\nLAWTON ( KFDX/KJTL ) — The Lawton City Council has announced Jari Askins is to serve as Interim City Attorney for the City of Lawton.\nIn this new role, Askin will oversee the Legal Department for the city and provide the City Council and administration with legal guidance.\nAs a Duncan native, Askin earned her Bachelor of Arts degree from the University of Oklahoma and has more than 40 years of experience in distinguished public service, including leadership roles in all three branches of the state government and as interim president of Cameron University, among many other roles.\n“Jari Askins brings a wealth of experience, professionalism, and wisdom to the City of Lawton,” said Mayor Stan Booker. “Her leadership will strengthen our legal operations and support our continued efforts to serve the citizens of Lawton with transparency and integrity. We are very proud to welcome her to our team.”\nWith Askin in the new role, Interim City Attorney Tim Wilson will return to the role of Deputy City Attorney as they continue to search for a permanent City Attorney.\n“We are fortunate to have an exceptional legal team — individuals who work together daily to provide sound guidance and uphold the highest standards of municipal law,” said Booker. “It truly takes everyone’s teamwork and commitment to carry the City through this period of transition, and I’m grateful for their continued service and professionalism.”",
